== savestate: a title run's disk is its golden profile, or none on a first-run
  ok   a returning run is prepared from the seeded golden (rc=0)
  ok     ... the seed proposed hdd.img's save as Crimson Skies' golden
  ok     ... hdd.json records title, state and the golden loaded (got: golden 7d1496b774d3)
  ok     ... and the device's disk carries Nathan
  ok   after the run, its save is harvested to latest
  ok     ... and the golden is still Nathan
  ok   VOID REPRODUCED: the device registry names the run's bare save, what the old disk carried next
  ok   the next returning run rebuilds (rc=0, plans: build keep)
  ok     GUARD: onto Nathan again, not the bare state the last run left
  ok   a first-run of the same title is prepared (rc=0)
  ok     ... its disk carries no Crimson Skies save
  ok     ... and hdd.json says so (loaded: none)
  ok   a returning run of a title with no golden is refused, rc 3 (got 3)
  ok     ... with the reason in hdd.refused
  ok     ... before any push, and hddPath never moved
  ok   a first-run that reached mark profile-saved makes the title's golden
  ok     ... and a returning run of it is now prepared, not refused
== savestate: request.sh refuses a route whose state the disk cannot match
  ok   VOID REPRODUCED + GUARD: a returning route with no golden is refused at the prompt
  ok     ... and nothing was queued
  ok   with Crimson Skies' golden it is queued, title_id and state in the request
  ok   a variant family resolves to .first-run for a title with no golden (route: burnout3 -> burnout3.first-run (4541005B has no golden profile))
  ok     ... and to .returning once it has one
  ok   serve_one passes the request's title_id and title_state to the prepare
  ok     ... and a refusal ends the request before the soak, with its reason
== savestate: a soak whose route dies stops, instead of holding blind
  ok   a route that dies (rc 2) stops a 30 s soak early (rc=6, 1s)
  ok     ... and says route-died in run.log
  ok   a route that ends cleanly (rc 0) holds the soak's window (rc=0, 4s)
